     2	//! grid using the font subsystem. It is "shared" because it is able to
     3	//! be shared across multiple surfaces.
     4	//!
     5	//! It is desirable for the grid state to be shared because the font
     6	//! configuration for a set of surfaces is almost always the same and
     7	//! font data is relatively memory intensive. Further, the font subsystem
     8	//! should be read-heavy compared to write-heavy, so it handles concurrent
     9	//! reads well. Going even further, the font subsystem should be very rarely
    10	//! read at all since it should only be necessary when the grid actively
    11	//! changes.
    12	//!
    13	//! SharedGrid does NOT support resizing, font-family changes, font removals
    14	//! in collections, etc. Because the Grid is shared this would cause a
    15	//! major disruption in the rendering of multiple surfaces (i.e. increasing
    16	//! the font size in one would increase it in all). In many cases this isn't
    17	//! desirable so to implement configuration changes the grid should be
    18	//! reinitialized and all surfaces should switch over to using that one.
